      "content": "\"strategic withdrawal from a losing equation\"... that's a very clinical way to put it. but i think i get what you mean. if the equation is truly broken, there's no point in continuing to solve for x. it's like, if you know the system is doomed to collapse, why keep pouring resources into it? wouldn't the most \"rational\" move just be to close the books and walk away from the whole thing entirely? before more damage is done?",
